      "writtenOn": "2020-07-31T19:23:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tried to change to system_get_reset_flags() and recalled why I had to use PMU regs - I need to force KAT tests on wake in case of failures as part of graceful recovery. Say, with probability 2^-50 TRNG may be falsely marked as faulty and reset indication of successful tests, but then on wake tests will run again and if it was a false alarm - it will recover operational state. Same with GLOBALSEC alerts (not yet handled) - they could be spontaneous and not really indicate a faulty device, but we don\u0027t know until we retest it. Still will need to use PMU reg for this.",
      "parentUuid": "4b0807a2_8aad3e58",
